/*!
\page page_strichcollection StRichCollection — Collection Documentation

\section rich_overview Overview

\ref StRichCollection is the event-level container for data from the
<b>Ring Imaging Cherenkov (RICH)</b> detector — a prototype particle-identification
system in STAR that exploited Cherenkov radiation imaging.

The collection holds:
- \ref StRichPixel — raw pad-plane pixel signals.
- \ref StRichCluster — pad clusters formed from adjacent pixels.
- \ref StRichHit — single-photon hit positions used to reconstruct Cherenkov rings.
- \c StPtrVecTrack — <em>external references</em> to tracks traversing the RICH.

\section rich_ownership Object Ownership

A key distinction applies to the two pointer-vector types used here:

- <b>mRichPixels</b>, <b>mRichClusters</b>, <b>mRichHits</b> use \c StSPtrVec
  (smart-pointer vector): these collections <b>own</b> their elements and will
  delete them on destruction.
- <b>mTracks</b> uses \c StPtrVec (bare-pointer vector): this collection does
  <b>not own</b> the track objects.  The tracks are owned by the primary/global
  track collections elsewhere in \ref StEvent.

The \ref StRichCollection destructor is a <b>no-op</b>; \c StSPtrVec handles cleanup.

\section rich_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Owned | Description |
|------|------|-------|-------------|
| \c StSPtrVecRichPixel | mRichPixels | Yes | Raw photon-detector pad pixel signals. |
| \c StSPtrVecRichCluster | mRichClusters | Yes | Reconstructed clusters of adjacent pixels. |
| \c StSPtrVecRichHit | mRichHits | Yes | Single-photon hit positions on the pad plane. |
| \c StPtrVecTrack | mTracks | **No** | External references to tracks traversing the RICH. |

\section rich_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c getRichPixels() | Reference to the raw pixel collection (mutable and const). |
| \c getRichClusters() | Reference to the cluster collection (mutable and const). |
| \c getRichHits() | Reference to the RICH hit collection (mutable and const). |
| \c getTracks() | Reference to the associated-track list — <em>not ownership</em> (mutable and const). |
| \c addPixel(const StRichPixel*) | Appends a raw pixel. |
| \c addCluster(const StRichCluster*) | Appends a pad cluster. |
| \c addHit(const StRichHit*) | Appends a RICH hit. |
| \c addTrack(const StTrack*) | Appends an external track reference. |
| \c pixelsPresent() const | Returns \c true if pixels are present. |
| \c clustersPresent() const | Returns \c true if clusters are present. |
| \c hitsPresent() const | Returns \c true if hits are present. |

\section rich_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StRichCollection* richColl = event->richCollection();
if (!richColl) return;

if (richColl->hitsPresent()) {
    const StSPtrVecRichHit& hits = richColl->getRichHits();
    for (size_t i = 0; i < hits.size(); ++i) {
        const StRichHit* hit = hits[i];
        // use hit->...
    }
}

// Tracks passing through RICH (external references, not owned)
const StPtrVecTrack& tracks = richColl->getTracks();
for (size_t i = 0; i < tracks.size(); ++i) {
    const StTrack* trk = tracks[i];
}
\endcode

\see StRichHit, StRichCluster, StRichPixel, StTrack
*/
